EPIC BREAKDOWN: Self-Service Report Export Feature
================================================================================

EPIC TITLE: Self-Service Report Export for End Users and Administrators
EPIC ID: EXPORT-001
INITIATIVE: REPORT_EXPORT
PRIORITY: HIGH

EPIC DESCRIPTION:
Enable end users and administrators to export filtered reports to PDF and CSV
formats with audit trail capabilities for compliance and usage tracking.

INVEST COMPLIANCE CHECK:
• Independent: Can be developed and tested separately from other features
• Negotiable: Format options and filters can be refined with stakeholders
• Valuable: Directly addresses user need for offline report analysis
• Estimable: Scope is well-defined with clear acceptance criteria
• Small: Broken into manageable stories (2-8 points each)
• Testable: Each story has clear Given-When-Then acceptance criteria

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
USER STORY BREAKDOWN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 1: Basic CSV Export for End Users
STORY ID: EXPORT-001
POINTS: 5
PRIORITY: HIGH

As an End User,
I want to export reports to CSV format,
So that I can analyze the data in spreadsheet applications.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I am viewing a report with data
WHEN I click the "Export to CSV" button
THEN the report data downloads as a CSV file with proper headers

GIVEN I have filtered a report
WHEN I export to CSV
THEN only the filtered results are included in the export

GIVEN the report has 10,000+ rows
WHEN I export to CSV
THEN I receive a progress indicator and the export completes within 2 minutes


STORY 2: Basic PDF Export for End Users
STORY ID: EXPORT-002
POINTS: 5
PRIORITY: HIGH

As an End User,
I want to export reports to PDF format,
So that I can share formatted reports with stakeholders.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I am viewing a report with data
WHEN I click the "Export to PDF" button
THEN the report downloads as a formatted PDF with headers and pagination

GIVEN I have a report with charts/visualizations
WHEN I export to PDF
THEN the visualizations are rendered correctly in the PDF

GIVEN the report spans multiple pages
WHEN I export to PDF
THEN page numbers and consistent headers appear on each page


STORY 3: Filtered Export with Date Ranges
STORY ID: EXPORT-003
POINTS: 8
PRIORITY: MEDIUM

As a Power User,
I want to export reports with custom filters and date ranges,
So that I can analyze specific subsets of data.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I am on the report page
WHEN I apply filters (date range, category, status)
THEN the export includes only data matching my filter criteria

GIVEN I select a custom date range
WHEN I export the report
THEN the exported file includes a timestamp of the export in the filename

GIVEN I apply multiple filters simultaneously
WHEN I export to CSV or PDF
THEN all filter conditions are applied correctly


STORY 4: Export Activity Audit Log for Administrators
STORY ID: EXPORT-004
POINTS: 5
PRIORITY: HIGH

As an Administrator,
I want to view an audit log of all report exports,
So that I can track data access for compliance purposes.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I am logged in as an Administrator
WHEN I navigate to the Export Audit page
THEN I see a list of all export activities with user, timestamp, and report name

GIVEN an export has occurred
WHEN I view the audit log
THEN I see the user ID, export format, report name, and timestamp

GIVEN I filter the audit log by user or date range
WHEN I apply the filter
THEN only matching export activities are displayed


STORY 5: Export Permissions and Access Control
STORY ID: EXPORT-005
POINTS: 3
PRIORITY: HIGH

As an Administrator,
I want to control which users can export reports,
So that I can restrict sensitive data access.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN a user has "Read-Only" permission
WHEN they view a report
THEN the export buttons are hidden or disabled

GIVEN a user has "Export" permission
WHEN they view a report
THEN the export buttons are visible and functional

GIVEN I am an Administrator
WHEN I modify user permissions
THEN the export capability updates immediately


STORY 6: Export Status Notification
STORY ID: EXPORT-006
POINTS: 3
PRIORITY: MEDIUM

As an End User,
I want to receive notification when my export is complete,
So that I know when to download the file.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I initiate a large export (>5000 rows)
WHEN the export is processing
THEN I see a "Processing" status indicator

GIVEN my export completes successfully
WHEN the export finishes
THEN I receive an in-app notification and download link

GIVEN my export fails
WHEN the export fails
THEN I receive an error message with retry option


STORY 7: Backend Export Service Infrastructure
STORY ID: EXPORT-007
POINTS: 5
PRIORITY: HIGH

As a Developer,
I need a robust export service backend,
So that exports are reliable and scalable.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN an export request is made
WHEN the service processes the request
THEN the export is queued and processed asynchronously

GIVEN multiple concurrent export requests occur
WHEN the service handles the load
THEN requests are queued and processed without data corruption

GIVEN an export times out (>5 minutes)
WHEN the timeout occurs
THEN the user receives an error and the job is cleaned up


STORY 8: Export File Naming Convention
STORY ID: EXPORT-008
POINTS: 2
PRIORITY: LOW

As an End User,
I want exported files to have descriptive names,
So that I can identify and organize my exports.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I export a report named "Sales Summary"
WHEN I download the file
THEN the filename is "Sales_Summary_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.csv" or ".pdf"

GIVEN I export a filtered report
WHEN I download the file
THEN the filename includes a hash or ID to differentiate filtered exports


STORY 9: UI/UX Export Button Integration
STORY ID: EXPORT-009
POINTS: 3
PRIORITY: HIGH

As an End User,
I want clear export buttons on report pages,
So that I can easily access the export functionality.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN I am viewing any report page
WHEN I look at the toolbar
THEN I see clearly labeled "Export to CSV" and "Export to PDF" buttons

GIVEN I hover over an export button
WHEN I hover
THEN a tooltip explains the export format and any limitations

GIVEN I am on a mobile device
WHEN I view the report
THEN export buttons are accessible and touch-friendly


STORY 10: Export Error Handling and Logging
STORY ID: EXPORT-010
POINTS: 3
PRIORITY: MEDIUM

As a Developer,
I want comprehensive error handling for exports,
So that failures are logged and users receive helpful feedback.

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
GIVEN an export fails due to data issues
WHEN the failure occurs
THEN the error is logged with full stack trace for debugging

GIVEN an export fails
WHEN the user receives the error
THEN the error message is user-friendly and actionable

GIVEN the export service is unavailable
WHEN a user attempts export
THEN a graceful degradation message is shown with retry option

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
